// en-kitt — the pacing of the car.
//
// The deliberate opposite of en-hal, on the same phoneme set, so the two are
// heard as two temperaments rather than two accents.
//
// The common mistake is to make this voice FAST. It is not fast; it is CRISP.
// Every syllable is fully formed and then finished with, which reads as brisk
// because nothing is ever held. Speeding it up loses the precision that is the
// whole character and turns a very capable assistant into a chatterbox.

name en-kitt
language en-kitt 8
language en 22

phonemes en

// SHORT, AND MORE CONTRASTED. Below default across the board, and the gap
// between stressed and unstressed is WIDER than English wants rather than
// narrower: this voice points at things. Compare en-hal, which does the reverse
// on both counts.
stressLength 165 165 168 170 200 205 215 225

// Emphasis is real and it arrives as level. He would like it noticed.
stressAmp 15 16 18 20 22 25 28 31

// Words close together — not run together. 1 keeps the boundaries audible while
// removing hal's air between them.
words 1

dictrules 8
